# ===== MailCopilot local development environment =====
# Copy to `.env` in the repository root and fill in the values you need.
# `.env` is git-ignored. Variables already present in the shell win over this
# file (dotenv never overrides), so CI values are unaffected.
#
# `vite.config.ts` loads this file, which means the values reach both the
# build-time `define` substitutions and the Electron process started by
# `npm run dev`.

# === Google OAuth (Gmail sign-in) ===
# The repository ships no Google OAuth credentials, so a self-built binary
# cannot sign in with Gmail until you supply your own client.
#
# How to get them:
#   1. https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#   2. Create Credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Application type: "Desktop app".
#   3. On the OAuth consent screen add the scopes:
#        https://mail.google.com/   openid   email   profile
#   4. Paste the client ID and client secret below.
#
# Note: for a Desktop client the secret is not confidential in the OAuth sense
# (it ships inside every binary; PKCE is what protects the exchange), but it
# must still stay out of version control — indexed credentials get revoked.
MAILCOPILOT_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
MAILCOPILOT_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# === Sentry (optional) ===
# Without a DSN the SDK starts disabled and nothing is sent.
# SENTRY_DSN=
# SENTRY_URL=
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# === Auto-updates (optional) ===
# MAILCOPILOT_UPDATE_URL=
